_publ_section_title
;\
Synthesis and crystal structure of
bis[(1<i>E</i>,6<i>E</i>)-1,7-bis(4-acetyloxy-3-methoxyphenyl)hepta-1,6-\
diene-3,5-dionato(1-)-\k^2^<i>O</i>,<i>O</i>'](methanol)dioxidouranium(VI)
toluene monosolvate
;
_publ_section_synopsis
;
The first uranium--curcuminoid complex,
[U(C~25~H~23~O~8~)~2~O~2~(CH~3~OH)]\\cdotC~6~H~5~CH~3~, features a uranyl(VI)
center coordinated by two monoanionic bidentate 4,4'-diacetylcurcuminato
ligands and one methanol molecule. The uranium atom adopts a distorted
pentagonal--bipyramidal coordination geometry, in with four O atoms from the
<i>\b</i>-diketonate moieties and one O atom from the methanol ligand define
the equatorial plane, while the two uranyl O atoms occupy the axial positions.
;
_diffrn_standards_number 0
